From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:55:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: Fail FLR when config space is inaccessible

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167008

If a device is in an error state, its config space may not be accssible.
Add additional check to validate if a device's config space is accessible
before doing an FLR reset.

Signed-off-by: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Helgaas <bhelgaas@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Benjamin Block <bblock@linux.ibm.com>
Reviewed-by: Niklas Schnelle <schnelle@linux.ibm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260805165518.794-5-alifm@linux.ibm.com
(cherry picked from commit ad05c16b290be93e0ff02151b22c5d137f655908)
Signed-off-by: Lee Trager <ltrager@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Fenghua Yu <fenghuay@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-01990
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-bos@6b9e740254ddf948e04dee36340bc83108740698
---
 drivers/pci/pci.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pci.c b/drivers/pci/pci.c
index 44a764deb7a4..466d73d3a627 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pci.c
@@ -4392,6 +4392,9 @@ int pcie_flr(struct pci_dev *dev)
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	if (!pci_dev_config_accessible(dev, "FLR"))
+		return -ENOTTY;
+
 	if (!pci_wait_for_pending_transaction(dev))
 		pci_err(dev, "timed out waiting for pending transaction; performing function level reset anyway\n");
 
